laurel 2771: camera step 2 on the Mi A3: rear IMX586/IMX582 RDI raw frames 1280x720 RAW10 into memory, fps line, kept frame over USB. The sensor tables (init 531 writes, 1280x720 mode 6 94 writes for the IMX586) are not in the kernel: laurel_cam_lib.h parses the stock mm-camera2 library /usr/share/firmware/laurel-camera/libmmcamera_laurus_imx586_{qtech,sunny}.so / imx582_qtech.so at run time (ELF32 .data = sensor_lib_t: init/resolution tables of 3000 x {u16 addr, u16 data, u32 delay} + trailer addr_type 2 / data_type 1, out_info, CSI lanes 4 settle 0x13, CID LUT VC0 DT 0x2b decode 2; root step scripts/laurel/root-camera.sh, never in git) and writes them in CCI bursts of consecutive registers (239 + 39 writes). MCLK0 24 MHz = GPLL9 main M/N 1/24 (vote + lock check; else 19.2 MHz + line). Clocks (laurel_cam_clk.c): VFE0 + VFE1 GDSCs, csiphy/timer 268.8 MHz from GPLL4 (Android's rate: settle 0x13 unchanged) or 200 MHz from GPLL0 (settle scaled), CSID1 200 MHz, VFE 403.2 (GPLL4) / 480 / 576 / 256 MHz by the PLL that locks, 18 branches each checked (CLK_OFF), throttle_rt_axi vote; all back at the end. CSIPHY1 v3.5 as D-PHY with the msm_csiphy.c 2-phase lane sequence (mask 0x1f, enable 0xd5, cfg values, clock mux 0x5c00124 = CSID1); CSID1 v5.0 (reset 0x7ffff, CORE_CTRL_0 0x32103 from camera_config.xml lane assign 0x4320, CORE_CTRL_1 phy 1, CID 0 LUT 0x2b, CID0 cfg 0x23) or its test generator; ISPIF CSID1 -> VFE0 RDI0 (reset 0x000f1fff, RDI mux 0x5c00028, CID mask, frame-boundary enable); VFE0 vfe48 reset 0x3f7, VBIF + QoS/DS of trinket-camera.dtsi, RDI0 -> write master 0 frame based (period 1, pattern 1), ping-pong of 3 buffers from the GPU pool (contiguous, below 4 GiB), REG_UPDATE per RDI0 reg update, halt with the VBIF clock forced. Apps SMMU identity for the VFE streams 0x420 (mask 0) and 0x421 (mask 2) via topaz_smmu_identity. No interrupt line: status words polled every 1 ms. Self-check = one 2 s capture after the root mount: 'LAUREL CAMERA: rear stream: 1280x720 RAW10 at N fps, frame M (kept for camframe), mean X, exposure L lines gain G, VFE errors ...' (simple AE every 4 frames: 0x0202 / 0x0204 with grouped hold), or 'rear stream: off: <why>' (no library, no pool buffer, SMMU, a clock, a reset; no frame in 1 s: CSID packet/ECC/CRC counters, CSIPHY/ISPIF/VFE status, then the CSID test generator through the same path decides sensor side vs back end). USB command server (sweet_usb.c 2005): camframe (new 1.5 s capture), caminfo, camread G O (binary 'LCF1' header + 1400 bytes; not logged), host op10tool camframe / scripts/laurel/cam-frame.sh -> RAW10 + PNG. sysctl kern.laurel_camera_stream. Kill switch camera=0 (step 1). A failure turns off only the camera RDI path. Docs: docs/laurel_sprout/camera.md section 8.

